+/data/local/tmp/copy-indirect-android \
+  --driver /vendor_extra/lib64/libvulkan_nouveau.so --transform /data/local/tmp/transform.spv
 ```
 
 `../native-vulkan-multiqueue.c` requires graphics family 0 with exactly two
@@ -82,6 +88,10 @@ configurations: two graphics, two graphics plus compute, compute create-info
 first, compute-only, two graphics plus two compute, and two compute-only queues.
 Each configuration is created and destroyed eight times; every queue races
 256 fill/barrier/fence submissions and checks all 1024 output words each time.
+The mixed configurations also move an exclusive buffer graphics→compute→graphics
+with matching release/acquire buffer barriers and binary semaphore dependencies.
+Compute copies the graphics-written first half to a differently initialized second
+half; the final graphics queue copies it to host readback and checks every word.
 This directly loads the ICD; Android system-loader/HAL coverage is separate.
 
